### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### SEGURIDAD
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### 26. STUDENT puede LEER los prerrequisitos -> espera 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subjects/{{tap201}}/prerequisites
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

> {%
    client.test("200 OK", () => client.assert(response.status === 200));
%}

### 27. STUDENT NO puede crear prerrequisitos -> espera 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subjects/{{tap201}}/prerequisites
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prerequisiteSubjectId": {{tap104}}
}

> {%
    client.test("403 Forbidden", () => client.assert(response.status === 403));
%}

### 28. STUDENT NO puede borrar prerrequisitos -> espera 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/subjects/{{tap201}}/prerequisites/{{tap101}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

> {%
    client.test("403 Forbidden", () => client.assert(response.status === 403));
%}

### 29. Sin token -> espera 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subjects/{{tap201}}/prerequisites

> {%
    client.test("401 Unauthorized", () => client.assert(response.status === 401));
%}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### BORRADO
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### 30. ADMIN borra el prerrequisito TAP101 de TAP201 -> espera 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/subjects/{{tap201}}/prerequisites/{{tap101}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

> {%
    client.test("204 No Content", () => client.assert(response.status === 204));
%}

### 31. Borrar un prerrequisito que ya no existe -> espera 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/subjects/{{tap201}}/prerequisites/{{tap101}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

> {%
    client.test("404 Not Found", () => client.assert(response.status === 404));
%}

### 32. Ahora TAP101 ya no es prerrequisito de nadie, se puede borrar -> espera 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/subjects/{{tap101}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

> {%
    client.test("204 No Content", () => client.assert(response.status === 204));
%}

### 33. TAP201 quedo con 2 prerrequisitos -> espera 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subjects/{{tap201}}/prerequisites
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

> {%
    client.test("200 OK", () => client.assert(response.status === 200));
    client.test("tiene 2 prerrequisitos", () => client.assert(response.body.length === 2));
%}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### OBTENER TOKENS DE KEYCLOAK (opcional)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Reemplaza TU-CLIENT-ID / TU-USUARIO / TU-PASSWORD por los de tu realm.
### Si el client es confidencial, agrega &client_secret=TU-CLIENT-SECRET.
### Cada peticion guarda el token en @adminToken / @studentToken automaticamente.

### T1. Token de ADMIN
POST http://localhost:8081/realms/siga-realm/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=TU-CLIENT-ID&username=TU-USUARIO-ADMIN&password=TU-PASSWORD

> {%
    client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.access_token);
%}

### T2. Token de STUDENT
POST http://localhost:8081/realms/siga-realm/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=TU-CLIENT-ID&username=TU-USUARIO-STUDENT&password=TU-PASSWORD

> {%
    client.global.set("studentToken", response.body.access_token);
%}

### T3. Ver los claims y roles del token actual
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
